Found on Windows 2026-11-22 (Windows 11 Pro 26H2 build 26300.9711, unreagent d4edd23 built with Go 1.27.0) while setting up the UE 5.8 example project.

The Toolkit's upstream HEAD 9f6a0f7 (2026-04-02, "restore UE 5.6 support ... uplugin 5.6.0"; also the commit unreagent-example pins) sets "EngineVersion": "5.6.0" in UELLMToolkit.uplugin. FPluginManager::IsPluginCompatible (UE 5.8 Runtime/Projects/Private/PluginManager.cpp:2688) treats a set EngineVersion that differs from FEngineVersion::CompatibleWith() as incompatible and calls PromptToLoadIncompatiblePlugin, a Yes/No message box. Under -unattended (the launcher's default) the box is answered No and the plugin is not loaded.

Measured:
- UE 5.8.4 (CL 58902052), unreagent -no-agent on the example project: log "Message dialog closed, result: No, title: 'UELLMToolkit' is Incompatible, text: The 'UELLMToolkit' plugin was designed for build 5.6.0. Attempt to load it anyway?"; port 3000 never opened.
- UE 5.7.4 (CL 51494982), disposable project, editor started directly with -unattended, the plugin's .uplugin set to "EngineVersion": "5.6.0": "LogPluginManager: Warning: Plugin 'UELLMToolkit' requires engine version '5.6.0' and may not be compatible with the current current engine version '5.7.0-47537391+++UE5+Release-5.7'", the same dialog answered No, no port 3000. With "5.7.0" on 5.7.4 it loads (all earlier probe runs).
- UE 5.8.4 with the EngineVersion line removed: plugin mounted, GET /mcp/status 200 with 43 tools 13 s after start, the bridge lists 45 tools over MCP, unreal_status answers connected, engine 5.8.4.

So the reference setup (unreagent-example on 5.7, submodule at 9f6a0f7) had no in-editor MCP under unreagent's defaults. The bridge smoke test still passes (it does not need the editor); only the 5-minute endpoint watch warns, and since the watch is a bare TCP connect (k205) nothing names the cause. README "Option B: UE LLM Toolkit" ("drop the plugin into the Plugins/ folder - done") does not hold for this plugin version.

Candidates for the owner (unreagent-worker, docs after): a startup check that reads the .uplugin of the Toolkit (or of every enabled project plugin) and warns when EngineVersion is set and its major.minor differs from the engine's, naming the fix (remove the field or set it to the engine version); the README Option B steps to say so. The unreagent-example 5.8 port removes the field; where that port lives (fork, upstream PR) is Getty's decision.

Upstream state 2026-11-22: ColtonWilley/ue-llm-toolkit PR #14 (Getty) drops the EngineVersion line on its own, open; upstream PR #13 (another contributor, open since 2026-07-10, mergeable) ports the source to 5.8 and keeps "5.6.0". Measured for #14: UE 5.7.4 with the field removed and -unattended: no dialog, plugin loads, /mcp/status lists 43 tools (run 46; the same on 5.8.4 with the port). Until upstream merges, unreagent-example pins the fork Getty/ue-llm-toolkit branch ue-5.8 (9fc7d4f, no EngineVersion). The launcher check this card asks for still matters: any other Toolkit checkout, and any plugin that sets an EngineVersion, hits the same silent refusal.

