Scope: every project plugin under <Project>/Plugins that the .uproject leaves enabled, not the Toolkit alone. Reason: the parse and the comparison are the same either way; finding "the Toolkit" needs either its name hard-coded or the bridge's directory layout, both brittle; and any plugin that sets an EngineVersion (a Fab plugin copied in from another engine version above all) is refused the same silent way. Enabled is approximated by what decides it for a project plugin in the common case: the .uproject's Plugins entry for the name (first one, case-insensitive), else the .uplugin's EnabledByDefault (absent = enabled). Not modelled, so no warning there (a miss, never a false alarm): target/platform allow and deny lists, a plugin enabled only as another plugin's dependency, plugins outside <Project>/Plugins (engine plugins, platform-extension and AdditionalPluginDirectories), plugins reached through a junction or symlink (Go's ReadDir reports a junction as irregular, not a directory; following links would need a loop guard).

Rule, read in the UE 5.8.4 source (E/ = Engine/Source/):
- E/Runtime/Projects/Private/PluginManager.cpp 1860-1864: every enabled plugin goes through IsPluginCompatible; on false, PromptToLoadIncompatiblePlugin (2709-2715, a YesNo FMessageDialog) decides; No -> "Skipping load of".
- PluginManager.cpp 2688-2706 IsPluginCompatible: an empty EngineVersion is compatible; one FEngineVersion::Parse rejects is compatible (warning "could not be parsed"); otherwise incompatible unless GetNewest(CompatibleWith(), declared) == Neither.
- E/Runtime/Core/Private/Misc/EngineVersion.cpp 162-197 Parse: three numbers (_tcstoui64, so leading white space and a sign are taken, no digits read 0) separated by '.', optional -CL, optional +branch, anything after the patch number ignored. "5.6" does not parse, so the engine loads that plugin.
- EngineVersion.cpp 56-91 GetNewest: major, minor, patch differ -> incompatible; changelists only when both carry one and both or neither are licensee changelists (bit 31).
- EngineVersion.cpp 199-208 CompatibleWith: (major, minor, licensee ? patch : 0, compatible CL | licensee bit). So on 5.8.4 "5.8.0" passes and "5.8.4" is refused; the fix to name is major.minor.0 (major.minor.patch on a licensee build), without a CL.
- Engine values: Engine/Build/Build.version, the file UnrealBuildTool compiles in (E/Programs/UnrealBuildTool/System/BuildVersion.cs 77 EffectiveCompatibleChangelist, 137-160 TryParse; E/Runtime/BuildSettings/BuildSettings.Build.cs 26-38). The installed 5.7.4 gives 5.7.0-47537391, which is what the measured log printed.
- Unattended answer: E/Runtime/Core/Private/Misc/MessageDialog.cpp 89-135 (YesNo defaults to No), 153-174 (under FApp::IsUnattended no box, the default is returned and "Message dialog closed, result: No" logged); App.cpp 274-279 (IsUnattended = -unattended or automation testing).
- Descriptor reading: E/Runtime/Projects/Private/RapidJsonPluginLoading.cpp 15-33 (first member matching case-insensitively), 200-234 (a number or bool converts to a string, which never parses as a version); E/Runtime/Json/Private/JsonUtils/RapidJsonUtils.cpp 9 (trailing commas accepted); E/Runtime/Core/Private/Misc/FileHelper.cpp BufferToString (UTF-16 LE/BE with BOM, else UTF-8 with or without BOM).
- Discovery: PluginManager.cpp 1120-1225 FindPluginsInDirectory (breadth-first; a directory holding a *.uplugin is a plugin and nothing below it is searched; directories named Content are skipped). Enabled: 421-435 IsEnabledByDefault (project plugin: unset = enabled), 1720-1756 (.uproject references first, then the enabled-by-default ones).

The card's candidate "major.minor differs" is too weak: the patch counts (5.8.4 is refused on 5.8.4). README Option B and the troubleshooting line say "major.minor" too: doc follow-up.

